vibeyard (https://github.com/elirantutia/vibeyard)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The agent terminal (milestone 03, story 02) adapts code from vibeyard, which is
licensed under the MIT License. The adapted pieces are the recipe — NOT the
package: the node-pty spawn-options block and the onData/onExit/write/resize/kill
lifecycle (win32-guarded), the CliProvider interface
(resolveBinaryPath / validatePrerequisites / buildArgs / buildEnv → pty.spawn),
and the xterm terminal-pane wiring pattern. vibeyard's Electron IPC carrier was
replaced with a WebSocket (`ws@8`) at /ws/terminal (ADR-003).

Files in this repository that carry the corresponding per-file vibeyard MIT
attribution notice:
  - src/terminal-ws.mjs
  - src/terminal-providers.mjs
  - ui/src/terminal/TerminalControl.tsx
  - ui/src/terminal/state-ramp.mjs
  - ui/src/terminal/geometry.mjs
  - ui/src/terminal/provider-picker.mjs

Milestone 46 unified the browser terminal: the board dock and the fleet card peek
became one control, and the four browser-side files that carried this notice were
replaced by the four above. The attribution TRAVELS WITH THE DERIVATION, so what
moved is recorded rather than dropped:
  - the xterm terminal-pane wiring (new Terminal / FitAddon / WebLinksAddon /
    open / fit / onData -> carrier / dispose) from ui/src/board/TerminalDock.tsx
    and ui/src/fleet/terminal-view/FleetTerminalView.tsx, which reached it
    through the dock, is now ui/src/terminal/TerminalControl.tsx;
  - the connection-state ramp from ui/src/board/terminal/dock-state.mjs is now
    ui/src/terminal/state-ramp.mjs;
  - the fit -> resize signal from ui/src/board/terminal/resize.mjs is now part of
    ui/src/terminal/geometry.mjs;
  - the provider picker moved unchanged to ui/src/terminal/provider-picker.mjs.
test/arch/acd-vibeyard-attribution.test.mjs parses THIS LIST and asserts it is
exactly the set of files carrying the per-file notice, so the two cannot drift.

